 75CU    NI(86KR,XG):XUNDL-1           2010DA06                           201003
 75CU c  Compiled (unevaluated) dataset from 2010Da06                           
 75CU c  Phys Rev C 81, 034304 (2010). See also authors' previous work          
 75CU2c  1999DaZQ: thesis by J.-M.Daugas, GANIL-T 99, 05 (1999)                 
 75CU c  Compiled by B. Singh (McMaster) and A. Negret (IFIN-HH, Bucharest);    
 75CU2c  March 10, 2010                                                         
 75CU c  {+75}Cu was produced following the fragmentation of                    
 75CU2c  {+86}Kr (60.5 MeV/nucleon) on natural Ni target (thickness 100 |mm)    
 75CU3c  at GANIL. The LISE spectrometer was used.                              
 75CU4c  B|r-|DE-tof technique used to identify the fragments.                  
 75CU5c  T{-1/2} of isomeric states was measured by storing the time difference 
 75CU6c  between the implantation of the heavy ions in Si detectors and the     
 75CU7c  delayed |g rays detected with four HPGe detectors.                     
 75CU8c  The assignment of spin and parities is based on the                    
 75CU9c  comparison with Shell Model calculations.                              
 75CU c  Level scheme is based on observation of 66.5-61.8 |g|g cascade.        
 75CU2c  Two possible scenarios are proposed: 66.5-61.8 cascade with            
 75CU3c  1/2- --> 3/2- --> 5/2- sequence, both transitions being M1+E2;         
 75CU4c  66.5-61.8 cascade with 3/2- --> 1/2- --> 5/2- sequence, with the       
 75CU5c  first transition M1+E2 and the other pure E2. Based on comparison      
 75CU6c  of experimental transition probabilities with those calculated from    
 75CU7c  shell-model calculation, 2010Da06 suggest preference for the latter    
 75CU8c  choice, which is given here.                                           
 75CU cL T$ From time difference between the implantation of the heavy          
 75CU2cL ions in Si detectors and the delayed |g rays detected with four HPGe   
 75CU3cL detectors (2010Da06) in Ni({+86}Kr,X|g)                                
 75CU cL J$ 1/2- and 3/2- doublet expected from large-scale shell model         
 75CU2cL calculations. The ordering of the two J|p's is from comparison of      
 75CU3cL experimental transition probabilities with                             
 75CU4cL those from shell-model calculations (2010Da06)                         
